there's a theoretical edge case

00:35:15.150 --> 00:35:20.160
of, what if 35 runs before 25?

00:35:20.160 --> 00:35:20.670
Right.

00:35:20.670 --> 00:35:22.837
Because we have to remember
that Shiny scripts don't

00:35:22.837 --> 00:35:25.490
run line 1 to line whatever.

00:35:25.490 --> 00:35:26.490
They don't run in order.

00:35:26.490 --> 00:35:28.230
They're more like dynamic.

00:35:28.230 --> 00:35:28.770
Right?

00:35:28.770 --> 00:35:29.730
Yes.

00:35:29.730 --> 00:35:32.470
So it may happen.

00:35:32.470 --> 00:35:32.970
Yeah.

00:35:32.970 --> 00:35:35.630
So if observe runs
first, now we're stuck.

00:35:38.850 --> 00:35:39.350
Yeah.

00:35:39.350 --> 00:35:43.370
So if 35 were to run before
25, then that would be bad.

00:35:43.370 --> 00:35:45.920
Can I bind this to
the diceval function?

00:35:45.920 --> 00:35:47.840
Like diceval has to be called?

00:35:47.840 --> 00:35:48.770
Yes.

00:35:48.770 --> 00:35:50.270
Diceval.

00:35:50.270 --> 00:35:51.500
Awesome.

00:35:51.500 --> 00:35:53.070
I think this will work.

00:35:53.070 --> 00:35:55.630
I'm going to stop it since I
think I crashed it last time.

00:35:55.630 --> 00:35:56.630
We'll get a clean start.

00:35:56.630 --> 00:35:57.650
OK.

00:35:57.650 --> 00:36:00.080
So we expect, when
we hit roll dice,

00:36:00.080 --> 00:36:03.620
that we're going to get not 3.

00:36:03.620 --> 00:36:06.380
We're going to just get
like new numbers here.

00:36:06.380 --> 00:36:08.360
So 1, so I shouldn't see 1.

00:36:08.360 --> 00:36:11.030
Got a 2, 3.

00:36:11.030 --> 00:36:12.910
All right.

00:36:12.910 --> 00:36:15.770
Look at that.

00:36:15.770 --> 00:36:18.073
That's so cool.

00:36:18.073 --> 00:36:19.490
This is such a
great example, too,

00:36:19.490 --> 00:36:21.710
because I was like, oh,
bindEvent would naturally

00:36:21.710 --> 00:36:23.850
bind to--

00:36:23.850 --> 00:36:26.100
almost what I would think
of as like a physical event.

00:36:26.100 --> 00:36:29.320
Like I'm clicking a button or
I'm seeing a physical change,

00:36:29.320 --> 00:36:32.250
but I can bind the event
to a function call.

00:36:32.250 --> 00:36:38.010
To any reactive value,
any set of reactivity.

00:36:38.010 --> 00:36:39.720
OK.

00:36:39.720 --> 00:36:43.320
And I think you can have
req statements in there.

00:36:43.320 --> 00:36:45.240
Stop.

00:36:45.240 --> 00:36:47.340
Just think of it
as, what would we

00:36:47.340 --> 00:36:51.910
do in the beginning of
that reactive expression?

00:36:51.910 --> 00:36:54.150
You can do lots of logic.

00:36:54.150 --> 00:36:56.970
You can hit lots of reactivity.

00:36:56.970 --> 00:36:58.500
All right.

00:36:58.500 --> 00:36:59.790
OK.

00:36:59.790 --> 00:37:03.510
I want to see what
people do with this.

00:37:03.510 --> 00:37:05.100
I want to see all
kinds of things.

00:37:05.100 --> 00:37:07.320
I want to see what you
can do with bindEvent.

